{"Title":"An Act relative to annoying telephone calls","BillNumber":"H1512","DocketNumber":"HD1347","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"CMG1","Name":"Colleen M. Garry","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/CMG1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-10T15:03:13.247"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"CMG1","Name":"Colleen M. Garry","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/CMG1","ResponseDate":"2023-01-10T15:03:13.2466667"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/H1512/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Representative Garry of Dracut, a petition (accompanied by bill, House, No. 1512) of Colleen M. Garry relative to the penalty for persons making annoying and abusive telephone calls.  The Judiciary.","DocumentText":"\tSECTION 1.  Chapter 269 of the General Laws is hereby amended by inserting after section 14B the following section:-\r\n\tSection 14C.  Whoever allows his telephone to be used by another to telephone a person or his family, repeatedly, for the sole purpose of harassing, annoying or molesting that other person or his family or for the purpose of repeatedly using indecent or obscene language to that person or his family, shall be punished by a fine of not more than $500 or by imprisonment for not more than 3 months, or both.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J19","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J19"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}